{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1772652245,"nonce":"bQM2YaYE8fVBsjbP/asR5fSKyYU=","title":"Edge positions stale after node reversal — edges not rebuilt in toggleNodeReversed","message":"When toggleNodeReversed() is called, it updates uiState and nodes but does not rebuild the edges array. Edges have their own sourcePosition/targetPosition fields that depend on the reversed state of their endpoints. These remain stale until another action triggers a full rebuild (e.g., a fold/unfold).\n\nFix: rebuild edges (via buildStateEdges or equivalent) inside toggleNodeReversed, same as uiState and nodes.\n\nFile: web/src/stores/graphStore.ts, toggleNodeReversed action.","files":null}]}